 ## Overview
-Coarse-to-Fine Model Initialization is a training strategy that initializes a high-resolution (fine) neural radiance field model using the optimized parameters of a lower-resolution (coarse) model [S1]. It shortens training time and improves performance by reusing the coarse deformation MLP weights and interpolating the coarse feature grid into the fine grid [S1]. It employs progressive scale training, doubling the voxel resolution after a set number of iterations [S1].
+Coarse-to-Fine Model Initialization is a training strategy that initializes a high-resolution (fine) neural radiance field model using the optimized parameters of a lower-resolution (coarse) model [S1]. It shortens training time and improves performance by reusing the coarse deformation MLP weights and interpolating the coarse feature grid into the fine grid [S1]. It employs progressive scale training, doubling the voxel resolution after a set number of iterations [S1]. Unlike [Hierarchical Spherical Harmonics Optimization](5444-hierarchical-spherical-harmonics-optimization.md) which refines spherical harmonic coefficients across scales, and [NeuTex Training Schedule](22533-neutex-training-schedule.md) which schedules texture atlas updates, this method explicitly transfers learned geometric and appearance priors from a coarse grid to a fine grid before continuing optimization.
 
